                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=31
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=31
>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                                                 ; to the round constant  which is where the cipher
                                                               ; begins
                                                               ; ASSERT zero 16:44
                                                               ; ASSERT zero 46:116
                                                               ; AES_128 ENCRYPTION  the rounds and nothing else  no
                                                               ; table and no input or output; ENTERED AT CELL 45 with
                                                               ; the key in the four word window at the block's own
                                                               ; zero  the plaintext already in the state  and THE S
                                                               ; BOX ALREADY IN THE TAPE; It leaves the ciphertext in
                                                               ; the state and the pointer at nought;
;
                                                               ; ENTERED AT 45 AND NOT AT NOUGHT  because 45 is where
                                                               ; block/aes128table leaves the pointer and cell 45 is
                                                               ; the round constant this file's first instruction
                                                               ; sets; The two were one file until a mode needed the
                                                               ; table laid down once and the rounds run many times;
                                                               ; Splitting them exactly there is what keeps this
                                                               ; instruction stream identical to the program it came
                                                               ; from;
;
                                                               ; A CALLER MUST HAVE RUN block/aes128table FIRST  and
                                                               ; must not run it twice; that file's header says why
                                                               ; and the short version is that the lay down is delta
                                                               ; coded against zeroed cells;
;
                                                               ; THIS EXISTS SO A MODE CAN HAVE THE CIPHER WITHOUT ITS
                                                               ; PROGRAM; aes/encrypt128 carries an unbalanced walk
                                                               ; and so has no INTERFACE line  which means no caller
                                                               ; can PASTE it; and it is a program besides  reading
                                                               ; key and plaintext from the wire and emitting sixteen
                                                               ; bytes; A mode wants neither of those: it wants the
                                                               ; rounds over cells it chose itself;
;
                                                               ; THE KEY IS SPENT; the schedule advances through the
                                                               ; window a word at a time and the round constant with
                                                               ; it  so a caller running a second block must put the
                                                               ; key back first  and must enter at 45 again with rcon
                                                               ; back at zero; That is the caller's business and it is
                                                               ; why this block does not try to keep a pristine copy:
                                                               ; a mode knows how many blocks it has and where it can
                                                               ; afford to keep one; Sixteen bytes against a hundred
                                                               ; and fourteen million is not a cost worth designing
                                                               ; around;
;
                                                               ; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE; every one of them is a claim
                                                               ; about a cell of THIS block  and the include's offset
                                                               ; resolves it; CONVENTIONS section 6 carries the rule
                                                               ; and tools/bfdag enforces it;
;
                                                               ; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero)
;   @0x000:0x00f  window{16}  four schedule slots; the key goes in here
;   @0x010:0x028  the schedule's paste workspace
;   @0x029:0x02c  temp{4}   @0x02d rcon   @0x02e g   @0x02f cnt
;   @0x032:0x061  aes/mixcolumns pasted at 50  state cells 82 to 97
;   @0x052:0x061  state{16}  the plaintext goes in here and the ciphertext
                                                               ; comes back here
;   @0x062:0x071  the round key  copied beside the state each round
;   @0x072:0x374  the S box  laid down by block/aes128table  READ ONLY here
;
                                                               ; THE ROUND CONSTANT MUST ARRIVE CLEAR; the first
                                                               ; instruction below is a plus sign on cell 45 and it is
                                                               ; meant to make the constant ONE; A caller running a
                                                               ; second block finds 0x6c there  because the schedule
                                                               ; xtimes the constant ten times and nothing puts it
                                                               ; back; That was measured on the Appendix B vector
                                                               ; rather than reasoned about  and the contract below is
                                                               ; what stops the next mode rediscovering it;
;
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=45
                                                               ; ASSERT zero 45:45
  +                                                            ; the round constant starts at one
  <<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=0

